{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":492229,"name":"Max Maldonado","username":"Max_Maldonado","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/a587f6/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T02:08:15.181Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492229-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492229-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492229-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492229-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot is completely stuck in a “Reset failed” loop and cannot connect to the backend computer on Windows.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCRUCIAL CONTEXT: This issue is strictly isolated to the Windows application. I have a dual-boot setup on this exact same machine, and Grok Bot works perfectly fine on my Ubuntu partition. It also works flawlessly on my mobile phone. This confirms my hardware, local network, and router are working correctly, and the issue is either a Windows-specific bug or a corrupted VM state tied specifically to my Windows session.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRetrying does not work at all. Troubleshooting steps already taken to isolate the issue on Windows:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eReinstalled Grok bot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCompletely disabled Kaspersky antivirus and its network/SSL traffic inspection.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eManually deleted the local \u003ccode\u003e.grokbot\u003c/code\u003e data folder to force a clean environment.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFlushed DNS and verified that \u003ccode\u003enslookup test.us8.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e successfully resolves the IPs.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTested on a completely different external network (mobile phone hotspot).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492229-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492229-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen the Grok Bot desktop application on Windows.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAttempt to connect to the bot environment.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick on “Recover computer” or “Retry Reset” when prompted.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eObserve the permanent “Reset failed… partial state” error loop.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eImportant Network/IPv6 Context I discovered:\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhen IPv6 is ENABLED on my Windows network adapter: The app gets completely stuck on the initial startup logo screen with the message “Grok Bot is having trouble connecting” (see attached image). It doesn’t even load the main UI.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhen IPv6 is DISABLED (and using custom IPv4 DNS like 1.1.1.1): The app bypasses the splash screen and loads the main UI, but gets stuck at “Can’t reach your computer” on the left sidebar (see attached image). From here, clicking “Recover computer” triggers the unsolvable “Reset failed” pop-up.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492229-screenshots-screen-recordings-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492229-screenshots-screen-recordings-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/8/0/80178056878802133c5041563ac0f0a9ba9d8208.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/ih9sZjBTNdc4zjeU7eNTynpqaVO.png?dl=1\" title=\"Screenshot 2026-09-15 205824.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/8/0/80178056878802133c5041563ac0f0a9ba9d8208_2_690x367.png\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-15 205824.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"ih9sZjBTNdc4zjeU7eNTynpqaVO\" width=\"690\" height=\"367\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/8/0/80178056878802133c5041563ac0f0a9ba9d8208_2_690x367.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/8/0/80178056878802133c5041563ac0f0a9ba9d8208_2_1035x550.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/8/0/80178056878802133c5041563ac0f0a9ba9d8208_2_1380x734.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"0A0A0A\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eScreenshot 2026-09-15 205824.png\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1917×1020 19.9 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/0/8/0838e478bf237c3f8922a6ea8dd0f5b1fd52ec15.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/1aJI6hN0Rjficnylirl6wprhn6Z.png?dl=1\" title=\"Screenshot 2026-09-15 210241.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/0/8/0838e478bf237c3f8922a6ea8dd0f5b1fd52ec15_2_690x388.png\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-15 210241.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"1aJI6hN0Rjficnylirl6wprhn6Z\" width=\"690\" height=\"388\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/0/8/0838e478bf237c3f8922a6ea8dd0f5b1fd52ec15_2_690x388.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/0/8/0838e478bf237c3f8922a6ea8dd0f5b1fd52ec15_2_1035x582.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/0/8/0838e478bf237c3f8922a6ea8dd0f5b1fd52ec15_2_1380x776.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"0C0C0C\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eScreenshot 2026-09-15 210241.png\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1917×1078 104 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492229-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492229-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492229-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492229-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot version 0.53.0.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492229-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492229-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T02:08:24.719Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":20,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":100.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171808,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-stuck-in-partial-state-reset-failed-network-dns-already-tested","display_username":"Max Maldonado","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138017,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-stuck-in-partial-state-reset-failed-network-dns-already-tested/171808/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":true,"can_vote":false},{"id":492292,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T05:02:13.630Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report and especially for testing on Ubuntu and your phone. That comparison is the key clue. I see both screenshots, the splash screen saying “having trouble connecting” and the main UI saying “Can’t reach your computer”.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn our side, the Grok Bot computer has been up and running the whole time. Your phone and Ubuntu on the same hardware can reach it fine, but the Windows app stopped sending requests to us. “Reset failed” here means the request never left your PC, so it’s best not to click Recover or Reset right now. Your Bots are safe.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEverything points to something on Windows intercepting HTTPS. Grok Bot uses its own certificate store, so any product that re-signs encrypted traffic, like Kaspersky’s “Encrypted connections scanning”, breaks it. Cursor, browsers, and curl keep working because they trust the Windows system certificate store. This also explains why Ubuntu on the same hardware and network is fine. One important detail is that fully disabling the antivirus often still leaves the scanning driver active, so just “turning off Kaspersky” might not help.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCan you check this and tell me what you see?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Edge or Chrome on Windows, open \u003ca href=\"https://api2.cursor.sh\"\u003ehttps://api2.cursor.sh\u003c/a\u003e. A blank page or an error is OK.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick the lock icon in the address bar, then Connection is secure, then the certificate icon.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCheck the Issued by field. It should be \u003ccode\u003eAmazon RSA 2048 M01\u003c/code\u003e. If it says Kaspersky or anything else, that’s the interception.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf yes, open Kaspersky, Settings, Security settings, Network settings, Encrypted connections scanning, and choose Do not scan encrypted connections. Another option is to add Grok Bot under Threats and Exclusions as a trusted application with Do not scan encrypted traffic.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit Grok Bot, right click the tray icon, Quit, then confirm in Task Manager there are no Grok Bot processes left. Start it again and give it a couple minutes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the issuer already shows Amazon and the problem still happens, please attach this file: \u003ccode\u003e%APPDATA%\\Grok Bot\\desktop-structured-log-spill.v1.json\u003c/code\u003e. Paste \u003ccode\u003e%APPDATA%\u003c/code\u003e into the Explorer address bar. It contains the app’s own connection errors from the last about 18 hours, which we can’t see from our side.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAbout IPv6, our servers only publish IPv4 addresses, so IPv6 can’t be the cause by itself. The difference between the splash screen and the sidebar depends on whether the app had a saved list of Bots to display, not on the network.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T05:02:13.630Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":15.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171808,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-stuck-in-partial-state-reset-failed-network-dns-already-tested","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://api2.cursor.sh","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-stuck-in-partial-state-reset-failed-network-dns-already-tested/171808/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":true,"topic_accepted_answer":true},{"id":493469,"name":"Max Maldonado","username":"Max_Maldonado","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/a587f6/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T04:59:41.025Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi Dean,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThank you so much for the detailed explanation. I checked the certificate for \u003ccode\u003eapi2.cursor.sh\u003c/code\u003e in my browser, and indeed, the issuer was showing up as Kaspersky Anti-Virus Personal Root Certificate instead of Amazon.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI went into the Kaspersky settings, disabled the encrypted connections scanning just as you suggested, made sure to fully quit Grok Bot from the system tray, and started it again. It is now working perfectly. I really appreciate you taking the time to explain the why behind this.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/1/b/1b0554a79d2086e350817808db646519b5ef2e5e.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/3R2jnM7G2EQWqI4EHe6kfc7X6XA.png?dl=1\" title=\"Screenshot 2026-09-16 235509\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/1/b/1b0554a79d2086e350817808db646519b5ef2e5e.png\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-16 235509\" data-base62-sha1=\"3R2jnM7G2EQWqI4EHe6kfc7X6XA\" width=\"663\" height=\"500\" data-dominant-color=\"E6E6E6\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eScreenshot 2026-09-16 235509\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e698×526 16.7 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T04:59:41.025Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":45.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171808,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-stuck-in-partial-state-reset-failed-network-dns-already-tested","display_username":"Max Maldonado","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],