quo;t log in to the computer","id":171384,"title":"Grok Bot doesn't log in to the computer","slug":"grok-bot-doesnt-log-in-to-the-computer","posts_count":3,"reply_count":1,"highest_post_number":9,"image_url":null,"created_at":"2026-09-11T19:05:24.718Z","last_posted_at":"2026-09-11T23:02:16.266Z","bumped":true,"bumped_at":"2026-09-11T23:02:16.266Z","archetype":"regular","unseen":false,"pinned":false,"unpinned":null,"excerpt":"ya lo resolvi, era el antivirus","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"bookmarked":null,"liked":null,"thumbnails":null,"visibility_reason_id":4,"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"like_count":0,"views":43,"category_id":6,"featured_link":null,"op_like_count":0,"has_accepted_answer":false,"posters":[{"extras":"latest","description":"Original Poster, Most Recent Poster","user":{"id":137370,"username":"Esteban1","name":"Esteban","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/e19adc/{size}.png","trust_level":0}},{"extras":null,"description":"Recent Poster","user":{"id":-1,"username":"system","name":"system","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/system/{size}/99069_2.png","admin":true,"moderator":true,"trust_level":4}}]},{"fancy_title":"Grok Bot desktop — cannot access computer; Recover/Reset fails twice (partial state)","id":171644,"title":"Grok Bot desktop — cannot access computer; Recover/Reset fails twice (partial state)","slug":"grok-bot-desktop-cannot-access-computer-recover-reset-fails-twice-partial-state","posts_count":3,"reply_count":0,"highest_post_number":7,"image_url":null,"created_at":"2026-09-14T16:51:31.465Z","last_posted_at":"2026-09-15T11:28:20.468Z","bumped":true,"bumped_at":"2026-09-15T11:28:20.468Z","archetype":"regular","unseen":false,"pinned":false,"unpinned":null,"excerpt":"App: Grok Bot desktop\nIssue: Cannot access computer — “Não foi possível acessar seu computador”. Bots are safe but cannot load. \nTried: \n- Restart PC \n- Logout/login \n- Check for Updates (does not work / unavailable in t\u0026hellip;","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"bookmarked":null,"liked":null,"thumbnails":null,"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"like_count":1,"views":40,"category_id":6,"featured_link":null,"op_like_count":0,"has_accepted_answer":false,"posters":[{"extras":"latest","description":"Original Poster, Most Recent Poster","user":{"id":137765,"username":"Laercio_Albuquerque","name":"Laercio Albuquerque","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/258eb7/{size}.png","trust_level":0}},{"extras":null,"description":"Recent Poster","user":{"id":87436,"username":"Colin","name":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_group_id":42,"primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","admin":true,"moderator":true,"trust_level":3}}]}],"summarizable":false,"has_cached_summary":false,"valid_reactions":["heart","+1","crossed_fingers","clap","laughing","open_mouth","confetti_ball","hugs","heavy_plus_sign","heart_eyes","sunglasses","cursor"],"accepted_answers":[{"id":492292,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T05:02:13.630Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report and especially for testing on Ubuntu and your phone. That comparison is the key clue. I see both screenshots, the splash screen saying “having trouble connecting” and the main UI saying “Can’t reach your computer”.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn our side, the Grok Bot computer has been up and running the whole time. Your phone and Ubuntu on the same hardware can reach it fine, but the Windows app stopped sending requests to us. “Reset failed” here means the request never left your PC, so it’s best not to click Recover or Reset right now. Your Bots are safe.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEverything points to something on Windows intercepting HTTPS. Grok Bot uses its own certificate store, so any product that re-signs encrypted traffic, like Kaspersky’s “Encrypted connections scanning”, breaks it. Cursor, browsers, and curl keep working because they trust the Windows system certificate store. This also explains why Ubuntu on the same hardware and network is fine. One important detail is that fully disabling the antivirus often still leaves the scanning driver active, so just “turning off Kaspersky” might not help.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCan you check this and tell me what you see?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Edge or Chrome on Windows, open \u003ca href=\"https://api2.cursor.sh\"\u003ehttps://api2.cursor.sh\u003c/a\u003e. A blank page or an error is OK.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick the lock icon in the address bar, then Connection is secure, then the certificate icon.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCheck the Issued by field. It should be \u003ccode\u003eAmazon RSA 2048 M01\u003c/code\u003e. If it says Kaspersky or anything else, that’s the interception.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf yes, open Kaspersky, Settings, Security settings, Network settings, Encrypted connections scanning, and choose Do not scan encrypted connections. Another option is to add Grok Bot under Threats and Exclusions as a trusted application with Do not scan encrypted traffic.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit Grok Bot, right click the tray icon, Quit, then confirm in Task Manager there are no Grok Bot processes left. Start it again and give it a couple minutes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the issuer already shows Amazon and the problem still happens, please attach this file: \u003ccode\u003e%APPDATA%\\Grok Bot\\desktop-structured-log-spill.v1.json\u003c/code\u003e. Paste \u003ccode\u003e%APPDATA%\u003c/code\u003e into the Explorer address bar. It contains the app’s own connection errors from the last about 18 hours, which we can’t see from our side.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAbout IPv6, our servers only publish IPv4 addresses, so IPv6 can’t be the cause by itself. The difference between the splash screen and the sidebar depends on whether the app had a saved list of Bots to display, not on the network.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"topic_id":171808,"url":"/t/grok-bot-stuck-in-partial-state-reset-failed-network-dns-already-tested/171808/5","accepter_name":"Max Maldonado","accepter_username":"Max_Maldonado"}],"has_accepted_answer":true,"can_create_shared_issue":false,"shared_issue_visible":false,"can_vote":false,"vote_count":0,"user_voted":false,"discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_id":null,"discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_url":"https://your-url.zendesk.com/agent/tickets/","details":{"can_edit":false,"notification_level":1,"participants":[{"id":138017,"username":"Max_Maldonado","name":"Max Maldonado","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/a587f6/{size}.png","post_count":2,"primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"trust_level":0},{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","post_count":1,"primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_color":"","flair_bg_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"admin":true,"moderator":true,"trust_level":4}],"created_by":{"id":138017,"username":"Max_Maldonado","name":"Max Maldonado","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/a587f6/{size}.png"},"last_poster":{"id":138017,"username":"Max_Maldonado","name":"Max Maldonado","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/a587f6/{size}.png"},"links":[{"url":"https://api2.cursor.sh","title":null,"internal":false,"attachment":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":1,"user_id":750,"domain":"api2.cursor.sh","root_domain":"cursor.sh"}]},"bookmarks":[]}